The shipped write path and the size of its key:

const raw = await redis.get("leaderboard:global");
const board: Record<string, number> = raw ? JSON.parse(raw) : {};
board[userId] = (board[userId] ?? 0) + points;
await redis.set("leaderboard:global", JSON.stringify(board));

$ redis-cli STRLEN leaderboard:global
(integer) 2097152

A reviewer proposes a hash with one field per learner instead: HINCRBY leaderboard:global <userId> <points>.

Statement: "With the hash, GET /leaderboard?top=10 can read just the ten best learners from Redis instead of all 40,000 entries."
